## The Shot List

The **Visuals** tab acts as your Director of Photography. It converts your screenplay into a list of specific camera
shots.

1. Click **Generate Shot List**.
2. The AI analyzes each scene and proposes a sequence of shots (e.g., "Wide shot of the city", "Close-up of Detective
Dante").

## Customizing Shots

Each shot card contains the prompt that will be sent to the video generation model.

- **Edit Prompt**: improved the visual description.
- **Camera Angle**: Change from "Wide" to "Close-up" or "Drone Shot".
- **Duration**: Set how long the clip should be (usually 3-5 seconds).

## Generating Video

1. Select the shots you want to generate (or "Select All").
2. Click **Generate Video**.
3. Choose your model (e.g., Kling, Runway, Luma).

> [!NOTE]
> Video generation takes time and costs credits. Be sure your prompts are accurate before generating.

## Reviewing & Regenerating

Once generation is complete, preview the video clips.
- **Keep**: If you like it, do nothing.
- **Regenerate**: If the AI got it wrong, tweak the prompt and try again.